[22.069433, "o", "\r\nPASSAGE_0032: '8.3 Nursing Mothers\\nIn animal studies, acamprosate was excreted in the milk of lactating rats dosed orally with acamprosate calcium. The concentration'...\r\nPASSAGE_0033: '8.4 Pediatric Use\\nThe safety and efficacy of acamprosate calcium have not been established in the pediatric population.'...\r\nPASSAGE_0034: '8.5 Geriatric Use\\nForty-one of the 4234 patients in double-blind, placebo-controlled, clinical trials of acamprosate calcium were 65 years of age or o'...\r\nPASSAGE_0035: '8.6 Renal Impairment\\nAcamprosate calcium is contraindicated in patients with severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance of ≤30 mL/min) .'...\r\nPASSAGE_0036: '10 OVERDOSAGE\\nIn all reported cases of acute overdosage with acamprosate calcium (total reported doses of up to 56 grams of acamprosate calcium), the '...\r\nPASSAGE_0037: '11 DESCRIPTION\\nAcamprosate calcium delayed-release tablets are supplied as an enteric-coated tablet for oral administration. Acamprosate calcium, USP '...\r\nPASSAGE_0038: '12.1 Mechanism of Action\\nThe mechanism of action of acamprosate in maintenance of alcohol abstinence is not completely understood. Chronic alcohol exp'...\r\nPASSAGE_0039: '12.2 Pharmacodynamics\\nPharmacodynamic studies have shown that acamprosate calcium reduces alcohol intake in alcohol-dependent animals in a dose-depend'...\r\nPASSAGE_0040: '12.3\\tAbsorption\\nThe absolute bioavailability of acamprosate calcium after oral administration is about 11%. Steady-state plasma concentrations of acam'...\r\nPASSAGE_0041: 'The volume of distribution for acamprosate following intravenous administration is estimated to be 72 to 109 liters (approximately 1 L/kg). Plasma pro'...\r\nPASSAGE_0042: 'Acamprosate does not undergo metabolism.'...\r\n"]
[22.069511, "o", "PASSAGE_0043: 'After oral dosing of 2 x 333 mg of acamprosate calcium, the terminal half-life ranges from approximately 20 to 33 hours. Following oral administration'...\r\nPASSAGE_0044: 'Gender:\\nAcamprosate calcium does not exhibit any significant pharmacokinetic differences between male and female subjects.\\nAge:\\nThe pharmacokinetics o'...\r\nPASSAGE_0045: 'Acamprosate had no inducing potential on the cytochrome CYP1A2 and 3A4 systems, and in vitro inhibition studies suggest that acamprosate does not inhi'...\r\nPASSAGE_0046: '13.1 Carcinogenesis, Mutagenesis, Impairment of Fertility\\nDietary administration of acamprosate calcium for 2 years to Sprague-Dawley rats at doses of'...\r\nPASSAGE_0047: '14 CLINICAL STUDIES\\nThe efficacy of acamprosate calcium in the maintenance of abstinence was supported by three clinical studies involving a total of '...\r\nPASSAGE_0048: '16 HOW SUPPLIED/STORAGE AND HANDLING\\nAcamprosate calcium delayed-release tablets, 333 mg are white to off-white, round, biconvex, enteric-coated table'...\r\nPASSAGE_0049: 'Storage and Handling\\nStore at 20ºC to 25°C(68° F to 77ºF); excursions permitted to 15ºC to 30ºC (59ºF to 86ºF) .'...\r\nPASSAGE_0050: '17.1 Information for Patients\\nPhysicians are advised to discuss the following issues with patients for whom they prescribe acamprosate calcium.'...\r\nPASSAGE_0051: 'Renal Impairment\\nA lower dose is recommended for patients with moderate renal impairment. Acamprosate calcium is contraindicated in patients with seve'...\r\nPASSAGE_0052: 'Suicidality and Depression\\nFamilies and caregivers of patients being treated with acamprosate calcium should be alerted to the need to monitor patient'...\r\nPASSAGE_0053: 'Alcohol Withdrawal\\nUse of acamprosate calcium does not eliminate or diminish withdrawal symptoms .'...\r\nPASSAGE_0054: 'Pregnancy and Breast Feeding\\n- Advise patients to notify their physician if they become pregnant or intend to become pregnant during therapy.\\n- Advise'...\r\nPASSAGE_0055: 'Relapse to Drinking\\n- Advise patients to continue acamprosate calcium therapy as directed, even in the event of relapse and remind them to discuss any'...\r\nPASSAGE_0056: 'Colvale-Bardez, Goa 403513, India\\nManufactured for:'...\r\nPASSAGE_0057: 'Mahwah, NJ 07430\\nPackaged and Distributed by:'...\r\nPASSAGE_0058: \"Indianapolis, IN 46268 USA\\nRefer to package label for Distributor's NDC Number\"...\r\n================================================================================\r\nDRUG: Acclean Chlorhexidine Gluconate 0.12% Oral Rinse (08c9d3dd-717b-0148-e054-00144ff8d46c)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[22.069598, "o", "PASSAGE_0000: 'untitled\\nACCLEAN is an oral rinse containing 0.12% chlorhexidine gluconate (1,1’-hexamethylene bis 5-(p-chlorphenyl) biguanide]di-D-gluconate) in a ba'...\r\nPASSAGE_0001: 'ACCLEAN chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse provides antimicrobial activity during oral rinsing. The clinical significance of chlorhexidine gluconate o'...\r\nPASSAGE_0002: 'Chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse is indicated for use between dental visits as part of a professional program for the treatment of gingivitis as cha'...\r\nPASSAGE_0003: 'Chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse should not be used by persons who are known to be hypersensitive to chlorhexidine gluconate or other formula ingred'...\r\nPASSAGE_0004: 'The effect of chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse on periodontitis has not been determined. An increase in supragingival calculus was noted in clinical'...\r\nPASSAGE_0005: 'General:\\n1. For patients having coexisting gingivitis and periodontitis, the presence or absence of gingival inflammation following treatment with chl'...\r\nPASSAGE_0006: 'Pregnancy Category B Reproduction studies have been performed in rats and rabbits at chlorhexidine gluconate doses up to 300 mg/kg/day and 40 mg/kg/da'...\r\nPASSAGE_0007: 'It is not known whether this drug is excreted in human milk. Because many drugs are excreted in human milk, caution should be exercised when chlorhexi'...\r\nPASSAGE_0008: 'Clinical effectiveness and safety of chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse have not been established in children under the age of 18.'...\r\nPASSAGE_0009: 'The most common side effects associated with chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinses are: 1) an increase in staining of teeth and other oral surfaces; 2) '...\r\nPASSAGE_0010: 'In a drinking water study in rats, carcinogenic effects were not observed at doses up to 38 mg/kg/day. Mutagenic effects were not observed in two mamm'...\r\nPASSAGE_0011: 'Ingestion of 1 or 2 ounces of chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse by a small child (~10 kg body weight) might result in gastric distress, including nau'...\r\nPASSAGE_0012: 'Chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse therapy should be initiated directly following a dental prophylaxis. Patients using chlorhexidine gluconate oral ri'...\r\nPASSAGE_0013: 'Chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse is supplied as a blue liquid in 4-ounce (118 ml) and 1-pint (473 ml) amber plastic bottles with child-resistant dis'...\r\n"]
[22.069682, "o", "PASSAGE_0014: 'Rx Only\\nRevised: December 2015\\nDistributed by (in US only):\\nHENRY SCHEIN, INC'...\r\nPASSAGE_0015: 'Your dentist has prescribed ACCLEAN chlorhexidine gluconate oral rinse to treat your gingivitis, to help reduce the redness and swelling of your gums,'...\r\nPASSAGE_0016: 'REF 112-6720\\nDIRECTIONS FOR USE: Swish one tablespoon (15ml) in mouth undiluted for 30 seconds, then\\nspit out. Use after breakfast and before bedtime.'...\r\nPASSAGE_0017: '\\ufeff\\nINGREDIENTS: 0.12% chlorhexidine gluconate in a base containing water, 11.6% alcohol, glycerin, PEG-40 sorbitan diisostearate, flavor, sodium saccha'...\r\n"]
